CPU: AMD Ryzen 7 7700X 8-Core, 16 thread
Motherboard: MSI PRO B650-S Wifi ProSeries
RAM:G.SKILL Flare X5 Series DDR5 RAM 32GB
GPU: Zotac Gaming GeForce RTX 4070 Super Twin Edge OC 
Storage: KingSpec XG7000 2TB NVMe SSD 
PSU: GAMEAX Rampage Series 1050W 
Case: GAMDIAS ATX Mid Tower 
CPU Cooler: Thermalrihght Assassign X120 Refined SE ARGB
OS: Windows 11
Approximate build date: April 2024
Approximate cost: $1500

This build was to centralize my digital infrastructure, such as files, gaming, media play, and lab experimentation. 
I researched extensively with YouTube videos, reddit posts, blogs, and window shopping to finalize the hardware components I wanted to use. I already had a USB to boot the OS onto the system once it was online.

## System Validation
After assembly, the system was validated by checking:
- Successful POST
- CPU and RAM detection
- Storage detection
- GPU detection
- Operating system boot
- Network connectivity
- Device/driver status
- System stability under use
